ort-term  reduction in prices but that ultimately  could lead to higher prices that is what  the naysayers are saying is going to  happen in all of this but the white  house is really counting on the fact  that this is something that is being  done in coordination with other nations  as you reported and we should point out  very quickly that the strategic  petroleum reserves are typically  released for things like natural  disaster or other  sorts of issues not usually to alleviate  prices as the president is doing right  now it's about a one-month supply and  this is a bit of a gamble for the  president but in consultation with his  team he believes it will work because he  believes this is a situation created not  because of policy but because of the  pandemic we're going to wait to hear  from the president he's going to be  speaking in the coming hours about this  where he's going to make his case to the  american people kimberly thank you for  that kimberly harkett live for us there  at the white house  well earlier i spoke to rudy baruti  who's the chief executive officer of  energy and environment holding he says  the coordinated move will bring some  level of stability to oil prices  basically president biden decision to  start releasing from the sbr  is a very good move and it is one of the  strongest moves to dampen inflation  threat  if  opec plus and the saudis will not or  were not willing to increase their  production president biden had  three choices uh one is to ask u.s shale  industry to start boosting their  production this is one to use some of  the strategic petroleum  reserves that are  around 714  715 million  so what they have released now is around  seven  and if this is accompanied by india  china korea that is going to give a  major  stability to the oil uh  prioritizes and will give the level of  all prices to an economical sustainable  way especially after what we have seen  in the covered time
 

